SupraLINUX integration review for KWayland 6.7.5

Official signed upstream sources remain unchanged. The authenticated Ubuntu
Debian reference retains epoch 4, four ordinary binary packages, SONAME 6,
public headers, CMake/pkg-config exports, QCH and all original symbol guards.
The inherited Debian patch continues installing the public xdgforeign_v2.h
header; it applies cleanly to the signed source.

Build inputs use exact eligible ECM 6.30.0-0supralinux3 and supplementary
Plasma Wayland Protocols 1.22.0-0supralinux1 artifacts. Ubuntu Qt 6.10.2 and
Wayland 1.24 providers remain in place; no replacement Qt is authorized.

BUILD_TESTING compiles all upstream manual clients enabled by the upstream
configuration. Upstream registers no automated CTest cases in this project;
CTest discovery and build outputs are retained. Manual clients, real Qt QPA
sessions, compositor, clipboard/input and hardware integration remain later QA.

The private installed fixture checks the public ConnectionThread, Registry,
EventQueue, compositor/region/surface/frame and Plasma window-management API,
including PID/UUID, properties/signals, Qt model changes/removal and desktop
state. It validates actual native protocol requests on its own temporary socket
without buffers or rendering. The actual Ubuntu SDK client and server first pass
in a clean Ubuntu baseline. Their immutable binaries are then re-run after the
normal APT upgrade. The unchanged client also runs against a server generated
from the candidate protocol provider; a consumer rebuilt from the installed
candidate verifies exact CMake versions. Qt and Wayland runtime versions, all
four package versions, SONAME and installed documentation/data are checked.
Every private server is reaped and its runtime directory removed.
